'''''Salix aurita''''', the '''eared willow''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=SAAU9|taxon=Salix aurita|accessdate=26 October 2015}}</ref> is a species of [[willow]] distributed over much of [[Europe]], and occasionally cultivated. It is a shrub to 2.5&nbsp;m in height, distinguished from the similar but slightly larger ''[[Salix cinerea]]'' by its reddish [[petiole (botany)|petiole]]s and young twigs. It was named for its persistent kidney-shaped [[stipule]]s along the shoots.
